        "original_id": "d0dd5307-5765-5161-9ba2-11b2beeae7a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Black Star Line\n- People: Marcus Garvey\n- Organizations: Universal Negro Improvement Association (UNIA)\n- Concepts: Back-to-Africa movement, Colonization movement, Black Zionism\n\nFacts:\n- The Back-to-Africa movement, also known as the Colonization movement or Black Zionism, originated in the United States in the 19th century.\n- The Black Star Line operated from 1919 to 1922 as a shipping line incorporated by Marcus Garvey and other members of the Universal Negro Improvement Association (UNIA).\n- Marcus Garvey was an organizer of the Universal Negro Improvement Association (UNIA).\n- The Black Star Line became a key part of Marcus Garvey's contribution to the Back-to-Africa movement.",
